? What makes a multimedia title interactive?
+ Behaviour responds to user input
- Every scene uses a photograph
- Every file has the same duration
- All content plays in fixed order
= Input affects the resulting presentation.

? Which control decides the next branch?
+ Flow control
- Colour control
- Font mapping
- Audio sampling
= Flow control directs the sequence.

? What is an event handler?
+ A function run for an event
- A bitmap colour table
- A physical display cable
- A library thumbnail image
= A handler carries out the programmed response.

? What does registering a listener do?
+ Connects an event to a callback
- Immediately plays every scene
- Permanently deletes the event
- Changes all object coordinates
= The callback is invoked when the event occurs.

? Which can trigger an event-driven action?
+ A user click or timer event
- Only a physical mouse click
- Only opening the source file
- Only the final rendered frame
= Events can originate from users or the system.

? What is a library instance?
+ A placed use of a definition
- A separate programming language
- An uneditable physical photograph
- A fixed display refresh rate
= Multiple instances can share a library symbol.

? Which widget suits a continuous range value?
+ Slider
- Static title
- Page heading
- Decorative border
= A slider lets a user choose within a range.

? What should a butterfly stage-click handler read?
+ Pointer position in stage coordinates
- Only the browser page title
- Only the library creation date
- Only the sound file extension
= Correct local coordinates identify the destination.

? Why clamp a butterfly target near the stage edge?
+ To keep the whole object visible
- To change its library definition
- To delete all repeated events
- To disable keyboard operation
= The target can account for the object bounds.

? Random route selection alone has which property?
+ A previous route may repeat
- Every route must appear once first
- The same route can never recur
- No completion event is needed
= Exclude the previous index if no consecutive repeat is required.

? What should Pause preserve for a route animation?
+ Current route and progress
- Only the window background
- Only the source filename
- Only the library menu order
= Resume needs the state at which playback stopped.

? Why test every route before random playback?
+ Randomness can hide an untested branch
- Randomness guarantees all routes work
- Only the first route can contain errors
- A route cannot be tested separately
= Deterministic branch tests expose failures.
